@startuml
title Scheduled Live Refresh and Historical Backfill
start
:Run one centrally paced scheduler slot;
if (facility catalog refresh due?) then (yes)
  :Call /carpark without facility;
  :Cache facility IDs and names;
else (no)
  :Select next work item within the shared request budget;
  if (live refresh?) then (yes)
    :Call /carpark?facility={facilityId};
    :Map MessageDate from Sydney local time to UTC Instant;
    :Derive sydneyDate from MessageDate;
    :Upsert newest sample into the matching ten-minute bucket;
    note right: Live ingestion does not mark historical coverage COMPLETE.
  else (history backfill)
    :Select facility and provider eventdate segment;
    :Call /carpark/history?facility={facilityId}&eventdate={date};
    :Map each MessageDate from Sydney local time to UTC Instant;
    :Group and upsert records by their actual Sydney date;
    :Record completion only when all provider segments
    required for the Sydney date have succeeded;
  endif
endif
if (provider request failed?) then (yes)
  :Set historical work to RETRY_WAIT when applicable;
  :Record retryAfter;
else (no)
  :Keep processing later scheduled slots;
endif
:Return;
stop

note right
  /carpark?facility=... supplies the latest occupancy record for live refresh.
  /carpark without facility supplies the catalog.
  /carpark/history is only for historical retrieval.

  MessageDate is Sydney local time without an offset. Convert it using
  Australia/Sydney and store the resulting Instant in UTC. Ignore the legacy
  `time` field. Group all records by the Sydney date from MessageDate, not by
  the requested eventdate.

  TfNSW documents eventdate as a date but does not specify its timezone or
  boundary behavior. Validate adjacent eventdate requests against MessageDate
  before deciding which provider-date segments complete one Sydney day.
  Do not seal a Sydney day as COMPLETE after a partial segment or an empty
  live response. Empty historical completion is valid only after all required
  provider segments have been fetched successfully.

  Every provider request, including catalog, live, and history, consumes one
  shared scheduler slot. Run no parallel upstream calls outside that budget.
  Backfill may take additional slots when a Sydney date spans provider date
  segments. Retry later through the scheduler; bucket upserts are idempotent.
end note
@enduml
